{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Therefore whoever kills Cain.</b> This is one of the verses that shortened their words and alluded but did not spell out — 'Therefore whoever kills Cain' is an expression of rebuke: 'So shall be done to him' — such-and-such is his punishment, but it did not spell out his punishment." "<b>Sevenfold shall be avenged.</b> I do not wish to take vengeance on Cain now; at the end of seven generations I will take My vengeance from him — that Lemech, from the sons of his sons, will arise and kill him. And the end of the verse, which says 'sevenfold shall be avenged' — and that is the vengeance of Hevel upon Cain — teaches us that the beginning of the verse is an expression of rebuke, that no creature should harm him. And similar to it: 'And David said, Whoever strikes the Jebusite and reaches the gutter' (II Samuel 5) — and it did not spell out what would be done to him, but the verse spoke in allusion: 'Whoever strikes the Jebusite and reaches the gutter and draws near to the gate and captures it, and the blind…' — and them too he would strike, because they said, 'The blind and the lame shall not come of David into the house' — 'Whoever strikes these, I will make him head and chief.' Here he shortened his words, but in Chronicles he spelled out: 'He shall be head and chief.'" "<b>And HaShem set for Cain a sign.</b> He inscribed for him a sign of His name on his forehead. Another reading: something else — 'Whoever finds me will kill me' — the beasts and the wild animals; but the children of men did not yet exist that he should fear them — only his father and his mother, and of them he was not afraid that they would kill him. Rather, he said: Until now my dread was upon all the animals, as stated, 'And your fear…' (Genesis 9), and now because of this sin the animals will not fear me and will kill me. Immediately, 'And HaShem set for Cain a sign' — He restored his fear upon the animals."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:44.048868385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}